# World Machine Review Routing Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Redirect generated review reports, freshness surfaces, source-gap output, and review queues from `The Research Spine` into `World_Machine` while keeping executable scripts centralized in `My_Data`.

**Architecture:** Add a review-vault routing boundary in `scripts/lib/config.mjs` that defaults to `WORLD_MACHINE_ROOT`. Retarget existing compatibility commands to use that boundary, preserving historical Research Spine files and keeping a single generated queue at `World_Machine/_Inbox/Review Queue.md`.

**Tech Stack:** Node.js ESM scripts, PowerShell wrappers, Obsidian markdown vaults, Node built-in test runner.

---

## File Structure

- Modify `scripts/lib/config.mjs`: add review-root helpers that point to World_Machine by default.
- Modify `scripts/pullers/research-spine-flow.mjs`: retarget document paths, metadata, and queue writes to the review root.
- Modify `scripts/system/source-gap-register.mjs`: read/write review-vault run-summary and register paths through the review root.
- Modify `scripts/system/audit-research-spine.mjs`: keep the audit pointed at archived Research Spine but suppress or reroute generated inbox behavior so it does not create active Research Spine review tasks.
- Modify `scripts/bridge/daily.mjs`: update labels/comments only where they imply Research Spine is active.
- Modify `scripts/run.mjs`: update help text so users understand the compatibility command now writes World_Machine review outputs.
- Modify `scripts/tests/research-spine-flow.test.mjs`: update fixtures and assertions for World_Machine routing and single queue behavior.
- Modify `scripts/tests/command-surface.test.mjs`: update source-gap/audit expectations where paths or messages change.
- Modify `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `04_Reference/Pull_System_Guide.md`, and `90_System/CLI Command Audit.md` if they mention Research Spine as the active output target.
- Modify `C:\Users\CaveUser\Documents\Obsidian Vault\The Research Spine\README.md`: add soft-archive notice.
- Modify `C:\Users\CaveUser\Documents\Obsidian Vault\The Research Spine\AGENTS.md`: add soft-archive notice.
- Modify `C:\Users\CaveUser\Documents\Obsidian Vault\World_Machine\README.md`: document new generated review destinations.
- Modify `C:\Users\CaveUser\Documents\Obsidian Vault\World_Machine\AGENTS.md`: document the single generated queue and link-only policy.
- Modify `C:\Users\CaveUser\Documents\Obsidian Vault\World_Machine\scripts\docs\World Machine Automation Script Guide.md`: update command outputs and remove Research Spine as active review layer.

### Task 1: Add Review-Vault Routing Helpers

